                  <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.25rem;font-size:22px">Dr. Emily Perry</h3>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p style="margin-bottom: 0;font-size:18px"">
                Hi, I’m Emily! I’m a Chamberlain Fellow at Lawrence Berkeley National Lab, having completed my PhD at UCL in 2024 on background mitigation for the LUX ZEPLIN (LZ) dark matter experiment and future rare event searches. 
                My current research focuses on leading low-energy nuclear analysis for LZ and developing THz calibration systems for ultra-sensitive detectors (e.g. SQUATs) to be used in experiments (such as BREAD) in the axion dark matter group. 
                I'm passionate about public outreach, and when I'm not at the lab, you can usually find me outdoors, hiking, and staying active.
              </p>
            </div>

