                <div>
                  <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.25rem;font-size:22px">Alain Fauquex</h3>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p style="margin-bottom: 0;font-size:18px"">
                Alain Fauquex is a PhD student in Physics at UC Berkeley working on Superconducting Quasiparticle-Amplifying Transmons (SQUATs). 
                His research focuses on designing, simulating, and fabricating superconducting quantum devices, particularly on scaling the number of devices per chip using new types of quantum circuits, simulations, machine learning, and improved fabrication methods. 
                He also develops hafnium-based Josephson junctions for SQUAT devices. 
                Before moving to the US in 2025, he completed an apprenticeship in the R&D department of Pilatus Aircraft, where he worked on the PC-24 business jet. 
                While earning his BSc in Physics at ETH Zürich, he worked as a cryogenic engineer in the Quantum Device Lab and as a research assistant in the University of Zurich’s dark matter group as well as the Paul Scherrer Institute's radioactive materials group. 
                In his free time he likes to mountaineer, forage, and cook.
              </p>
