              <p style="margin-bottom: 0;font-size:18px"">
                Penelope is a mechanical engineer specializing in superconducting magnet design, currently pursuing a PhD as part of the AS&T Program at the University of California, Berkeley. 
                Her doctoral research focuses on the design of high-temperature superconducting (HTS) magnets for axion dark matter search experiments. 
                Prior to her PhD, she worked as an Electromechanical Engineer Fellow at CERN, where she led mechanical analysis during the production and testing of MQXF quadrupole magnets for the High-Luminosity LHC upgrade. 
                She holds a Master's degree in Automotive Engineering from the Università degli Studi di Modena e Reggio Emilia and a Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering from Politecnico di Torino.
              </p>
